new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8baa04
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/mcserver-neoforge-port.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# MCServer NeoForge community port
+
+This fork targets Minecraft 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.256 and Java 21. Its Apple Silicon native baseline is macOS 14.5 / Apple M1 with an ARM64 JVM. It is a separate community port of the public YSM 3.0 development sources; the upstream 1.20.1 Forge branch remains the reference baseline. Documents describing upstream test counts or Forge observations are inherited evidence, not acceptance results for this fork.
+
+## Scope and release boundary
+
+The operator requested Mac rendering with existing server authentication and model distribution retained. This requires the same YSM 3.0 protocol implementation on the server and participating desktop clients. A 2.6.5 Java JAR and a 3.0 native library cannot be mixed. No binary is production-ready until the acceptance checks below pass. The MCServer mobile distribution always excludes YSM. Server installation, restart and public modpack publication are separately deferred.
+
+## Host integration
+
+NeoForge persistent data attachments replace Forge entity capabilities. Shared model/auth/star state retains its NBT field names; client animation attachments remain transient and entity-owned. Join initializes required state, cloning initializes the replacement entity before moving state, and read-only lookups never create an animation runtime for every vanilla entity. Client-only attachment registration is isolated from dedicated-server initialization.
+
+NeoForge optional play payloads transport the existing bounded YSM frame bytes. The adapter keeps dispatch on the network executor and preserves each handler's owner-thread enqueue and exact-connection identity. The envelope is bounded below NeoForge's serverbound payload limit. The compression marker recognizes actual clientbound and serverbound custom payload records.
+
+Minecraft 1.21 rendering uses the new vertex consumer methods, matrix stack, skin access, enchantment holders and GUI layer events. The vanilla entity fast path stages native vertex output before committing to `ByteBufferBuilder`; failed native output leaves the mesh unchanged. Extended shader formats use their ordinary vertex consumer hooks. The obsolete 1.20 Embeddium buffer Mixin is not applied on NeoForge; current Sodium compatibility requires runtime testing. Iris integration targets the 1.21.1 Iris PBR namespace, not Forge Oculus.
+
+Optional compile dependencies are not bundled as gameplay mods. Resharped uses the component-backed `BladeStateAccess`; Forge-only legacy SlashBlade unsafe field access is retained only in the separate upstream baseline. Maid uses NeoForge payload records. SWEM uses its 1.21 entity type. Compilation alone does not certify these optional integrations.
+
+## Verification
+
+`compileJava` and `compileTestJava` check all Java and test sources. `portableTest` checks Mac architecture/version/extraction, Minecraft compression envelopes and configured Mixin members/invocations against the pinned host bytecode. It deliberately disables automatic JNI loading and does not replace `test` or `check`. The frame compression tests require JNI and remain in the full test suite.
+
+Full acceptance requires fresh native builds and tests on both desktop platforms, full Java/JNI tests, builtin materialization, dedicated-server and client startup, model import/catalog selection, cross-platform state synchronization, reconnect/resource cleanup, YSM-disabled client connection, Iris/DH render passes and actual Mac gameplay. These remain pending until independently observed. Existing upstream first-person/layer limitations and other unresolved development features remain applicable; see [support status](status/support-and-verification.md).
